# Which snip-36-prover-backend release strkd bundles into the desktop app.
#
# Single source of truth for the prover version, read by the CI release workflow
# and the staging scripts.
#
# ── PINNED TO v1.4.2 (deps-v16) — V2 / PROOF2 — CONFIRMED on Sepolia (2026-11-13) ──
#   Sepolia and Mainnet both run 0.14.4 and accept V2 (PROOF2) proofs:
#   snip-36-prover-backend v1.4.1 passed its counter + L2->L1 messages e2e on
#   both networks (2026-11-10; Sepolia block 17945639, Mainnet block 17763417).
#   v1.4.2 ships the reviewed low-memory port of the V2 prover (PR #153; proof
#   bytes identical to stock V2). Sequencer 148de445, proving-utils 0a97f45a,
#   V2 proving e0035ffc. Sierra compiler 2.19.0-rc.3 -> 2.19.6.
#   The virtual-OS program hash changed with V2 (v1.4.1 reports
#   0x1c7be3225dfb33359b3ba9ffbe1542b7da27879b6d89f47b967e512463fd324).
#   Live-verified with the staged darwin-arm64 release: a STRK20 private
#   transfer (test seed, account 1 -> 0, submitted by account 0) proved on-device
#   in 16-19 s at ~2.4 GB peak RSS and was accepted on Sepolia as PROOF2, with
#   the program hash above (block 18077302, tx
#   0x58069de49658a203a6dd090fde6e3cd22d43619cbc6975f99790ade661bc1ee).
#
#   v1.3.1 (deps-v13), PROOF1, CONFIRMED on Sepolia 2026-10-27:
#   v1.3.1 rebuilds the v1.3.0 prover with the low-memory hardening from
#   snip-36-prover-backend #143 (madvise uses the kernel page size; pooled iFFT
#   buffers are length-checked). Same pins and sequencer, byte-identical proofs.
#   Live-verified 2026-10-27 with the staged darwin-arm64 release: a STRK20
#   private transfer proved on-device (16.3 s, 2.06 GB peak RSS) and accepted on
#   Sepolia as PROOF1 (block 17234440, tx
#   0x253e8a21ad64796abd4286911a3a065acd8da94a5d87fcf801ea0d2425b1d24).
#
#   v1.3.0 (deps-v12), CONFIRMED on Sepolia 2026-10-26:
#   v1.3.0 builds starknet_transaction_prover with the low-memory prover
#   (snip-36-prover-backend vendor/low-memory-prover, PRs #128 + #140). Sequencer
#   e6b6fd2e (was 9f78ee7c), which pins the same prover revisions; still PROOF1,
#   byte-identical proofs, peak memory ~14 GB -> ~2-3 GB. Live-verified 2026-10-26
#   with the staged darwin-arm64 release: a STRK20 private transfer was proved
#   on-device (14.3 s, 2.05 GB peak RSS) and accepted on Sepolia as PROOF1
#   (block 17191935, tx
#   0x796c14410a1d20a33b0655b5496b7471864f91a0c0752350821fd0dca418184).
#   Pin before that: v1.2.2 / deps-v7 (live-verified on Sepolia 0.14.3, 2026-07-02).
#
#   PROOF1 is gone: the 0.14.4 networks moved to V2, and starkware-libs/sequencer
#   accepts only V2 proofs from 0.14.5 (#15240).
#
#   Before the NEXT bump: re-confirm the same two things on the live network —
#     1. the release parses the current block headers (prove a recent Sepolia tx);
#     2. the current Sepolia verifier accepts its proof (prove + submit a
#        proof-carrying invoke on-chain).
#   If a future release regresses either, file a snip-36-prover-backend issue and
#   pin back to the last confirmed-good version.
#
# STAGING: v1.2.x+ PREBUILT binaries are relocatable (unlike v1.1.3, which had to be
# built from source + patched), so stage-prover-prebuilt.sh is the fast path.
# `snip36 setup --prebuilt` pulls the deps set matched to the CLI (deps-v16 for
# v1.4.2). stage-prover-source.sh still works but is the slow (~30-40 min) path.
#
# See docs/project/status.md and memory prover-proof-format-pin / strkd-dinner-merge.
#
# Releases: https://github.com/starknet-innovation/snip-36-prover-backend/releases
SNIP36_REPO=starknet-innovation/snip-36-prover-backend
SNIP36_RELEASE=v1.4.2

# ── Integrity pins (independent of the release's own SHA256SUMS) ─────────────
# stage-prover-prebuilt.sh refuses to stage anything that doesn't match these.
# They were computed 2026-11-12 from the v1.4.2 release assets (deps-v16), and
# matched both releases' published SHA256SUMS at that time. A release asset
# swapped later (or a moved tag) fails the build rather than shipping. Bumping
# SNIP36_RELEASE means recomputing them: download the assets, verify them
# against SHA256SUMS and a live prove (see the checklist above), then hash the
# files listed below.
#
# Commit the v1.4.2 tag pointed at. sample-input/ is fetched at this commit,
# not the tag.
SNIP36_COMMIT=3a2bc73774eca3d96052db937a98c95057fef661

# snip36-<platform>.tar.gz (the CLI tarball, verified before extraction).
SNIP36_CLI_TARBALL_SHA256_darwin_arm64=f9c9274dc43329381ef00e10b2421b825c6ac958775a70d2fb202523e59f00e8
SNIP36_CLI_TARBALL_SHA256_linux_x86_64=945a4b04a84592e9fc09388b1321c5c5e8eb68515b8aab3b21221cd894180f26

